body:
Thanks, the fix looks good. I have also encountered another bug while testing the `IsValidHexNumber` method that we could fix at the same time.

Looks like GitHub struggled with suggestions in unchanged lines and messed up the diff rendering, so here's a proper diff:

```diff
diff --git a/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/StringExtensions.cs b/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/StringExtensions.cs
index 9765c0c3892..42413eb5d88 100644
--- a/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/StringExtensions.cs
+++ b/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/StringExtensions.cs
@@ -935,11 +935,14 @@ namespace Godot
             {
                 if (instance.Length < 3)
                     return false;
-                if (instance[from] != '0' || instance[from + 1] != 'x' || instance[from + 1] != 'X')
+                if (instance[from] != '0' || (instance[from + 1] != 'x' && instance[from + 1] != 'X'))
                     return false;
                 from += 2;
             }
 
+            if (from == instance.Length)
+                return false;
+
             for (int i = from; i < instance.Length; i++)
